Aziz, played by Robert Davi.

10
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:06,000
Mohammed, played by Geoffrey Arend.

11
00:45:06,000 --> 00:45:12,000
An American Carol (released as Big Fat Important Movie in other territories) is a 2008 American satirical
comedy film directed by David Zucker and written by Zucker, Myrna Sokoloff and Lewis Friedman.

12
00:49:12,000 --> 00:49:18,000
Using the framework of Charles Dickens' 1843 novella A Christmas Carol, the film follows liberal filmmaker Michael Malone (a
parody of Michael Moore) as he is visited by three spirits to teach him the importance of Independence Day.

13
00:53:18,000 --> 00:53:24,000
The film satirizes liberalism in the United States,
with focus on Moore's documentaries.

14
00:57:24,000 --> 00:57:30,000
It stars Kevin Farley as Malone, alongside an ensemble supporting cast that includes
Kelsey Grammer, Leslie Nielsen, Trace Adkins, Robert Davi, and Jon Voight.

15
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:36,000
Theatrically released on October 3, 2008, by Vivendi Entertainment, An American Carol received
negative reviews from most critics, who found the film's humor and satire to be ineffective.

16
01:05:36,000 --> 01:05:42,000
It also was a failure at the box office grossing only $7
million against a $20 million budget.

17
01:09:42,000 --> 01:09:48,000
The film marked the final onscreen appearance by Dennis Hopper before his death in 2010, and the last
collaboration between Zucker and Leslie Nielsen before the latters death in the same year.

18
01:13:48,000 --> 01:13:54,000
The film explores themes of parody, terrorism,
documentary filmmaking, absurd, dubious.

19
01:17:54,000 --> 01:18:00,000
The tone is lighthearted.
